---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AdBanner from '../components/AdBanner.astro';
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n';
const tutorialUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/tutorial/');
const pluginsUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/plugins/');
---
<Base
  title="DeepSeek Harness Install & Download — Official Channels + One-Line Setup (Windows / macOS / Linux / WSL) | dshbase"
  description="How to install and download DeepSeek Harness (DSH): official release channels (npm @deepseek-ai/dsh / GitHub source), version and SHA integrity checks, plus one-line install for Windows, macOS, Linux, WSL. Requires Node.js — then npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web."
  currentPath="/install/"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does DeepSeek Harness have an official installer (.exe / .dmg)?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "No. DeepSeek Harness ships only as a Node.js package (@deepseek-ai/dsh on npm) and as source on GitHub. There is no standalone Windows or macOS installer — any site offering a 'DSH installer download' is unofficial." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "What is the difference between downloading and installing DeepSeek Harness?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Downloading means fetching the package (npm tarball or GitHub source); installing means getting Node.js plus the dsh command in place. The official flow merges both: npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web downloads and runs the latest build automatically." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "How do I verify the integrity of a downloaded DSH package?",
        acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Run npm view @deepseek-ai/dsh dist.integrity to see the SHA-512 hash for the current release. Packages installed via npm or npx are verified automatically by the npm client; compare sha512sum manually only for tarballs from other channels." }
      }
    ]
  })} />
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Install · Download</p>
    <h1>How to Install & Download DeepSeek Harness <span class="accent">(DSH)</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">DeepSeek Harness is a Node.js package — the only requirement is Node.js. Check the official download channels and integrity verification first, then pick your system for a one-line install, or build from source. After install, see the <a href="/blog/dsh-rc8/">rc.8 hub</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>Downloading DeepSeek Harness: official channels</h2>
    <p>DSH has <strong>no standalone .exe / .dmg installer</strong> — any third-party "DSH installer download" is unofficial. There are exactly two official channels:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>npm release</strong>: package <code>@deepseek-ai/dsh</code> (currently <strong>0.1.1-rc.2</strong>, developer preview). Install commands below; to grab the tarball directly: <a href="https://registry.npmjs.org/@deepseek-ai/dsh/-/dsh-0.1.1-rc.2.tgz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">registry.npmjs.org/@deepseek-ai/dsh/-/dsh-0.1.1-rc.2.tgz</a> (swap the version to pin another).</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub source</strong>: <a href="https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness</a> — Releases publish tagged archives (<code>dsh-v…</code> tags).</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>Version &amp; SHA verification</strong>:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npm view @deepseek-ai/dsh dist.integrity   # sha512-… integrity value
npm view @deepseek-ai/dsh version          # latest release number</code></pre>
    <p>Packages pulled via <code>npm install</code> / <code>npx</code> are checksummed automatically by the npm client against the registry's SHA-512; manual <code>sha512sum</code> comparison is only needed for tarballs from other channels.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You need <strong>Node.js LTS (18+)</strong> — every script below checks for it first.</li>
      <li>DeepSeek Harness is in <strong>developer preview</strong> — iterating fast, <strong>breaking changes will come</strong>.</li>
      <li>Prefer an offline copy? <a href="/deepseek-harness-guide.pdf">Download the DeepSeek Harness guide PDF</a> (install · plugins · troubleshooting · vs Claude Code).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Windows — one line (PowerShell)</h2>
    <p>Open <strong>PowerShell</strong> (right-click Start → Terminal) and paste:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>if (-not (Get-Command node -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) &#123; winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS &#125;
npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code></pre>
    <p>If <code>winget</code> isn't available, install Node.js manually from <a href="https://nodejs.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nodejs.org</a> (LTS installer), then run <code>npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code>.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">macOS — one line (Terminal)</h2>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>command -v node &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || brew install node
npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code></pre>
    <p>If you don't have <a href="https://brew.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Homebrew</a>, install it first, or grab Node.js from nodejs.org.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Linux — one line (bash)</h2>
    <p>Debian / Ubuntu (uses NodeSource):</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>command -v node &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || (curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_lts.x | sudo -E bash - &amp;&amp; sudo apt-get install -y nodejs)
npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code></pre>
    <p>Other distros, or to avoid <code>sudo</code>, use <a href="https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nvm</a> then <code>npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code>.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">WSL (Ubuntu on WSL) — one line</h2>
    <p>Inside your WSL Ubuntu terminal:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>command -v node &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 || (curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_lts.x | sudo -E bash - &amp;&amp; sudo apt-get install -y nodejs)
npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code></pre>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Build from source (all platforms)</h2>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>git clone https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness.git
cd deepseek-harness
pnpm install
pnpm run build
pnpm dsh web</code></pre>
    <p>Uses <code>pnpm</code> — install with <code>npm install -g pnpm</code> if you don't have it.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Verify it's running</h2>
    <p>Open <strong><code>http://127.0.0.1:3080</code></strong> and enter your DeepSeek API key. To use a different port, pass it to the app:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web --port 8080</code></pre>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Install as a global command</h2>
    <p><code>npx</code> re-resolves the package on every launch. For repeated use — especially CLI / headless sessions — install the <code>dsh</code> command once:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh
dsh --version   # e.g. 0.1.0-rc.6
dsh web</code></pre>
    <p>Make sure npm's global bin directory is on your <code>PATH</code> (find it with <code>npm prefix -g</code>). If you run a portable Node.js without a global install, point npm's <code>prefix</code> at a folder you control (<code>npm config set prefix D:\dsh\npm-global</code>) and add both the Node and global <code>bin</code> folders to your user PATH.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Configure the API key</h2>
    <p>The Web UI stores keys under <strong>Settings &rarr; Models</strong>. For CLI / headless use, put the key in <code>$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml</code> (default <code>~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml</code>):</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>DEEPSEEK_API_KEY: sk-your-key-here</code></pre>
    <p>On macOS / Linux, set the file to <code>chmod 600</code> — DSH refuses a credentials file other users can read. The <code>DEEPSEEK_API_KEY</code> environment variable also works and takes precedence.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">Troubleshooting the install</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><code>ERR_PNPM_FETCH_404</code> / package not found</strong> — your default npm registry mirror may lag behind the official one. Retry with <code>--registry=https://registry.npmjs.org</code>.</li>
      <li><strong><code>'pnpm' is not recognized</code></strong> — the plugin manager forwards to pnpm; install it with <code>npm install -g pnpm</code>.</li>
      <li><strong><code>node: command not found</code></strong> — Node.js isn't on your PATH. Add your Node folder (and npm global bin) to PATH.</li>
      <li><strong>Port 3080 already in use</strong> — start on another port: <code>dsh web --port 8080</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <AdBanner variant="banner" />
    <h2 style="margin-top:24px">What to do next</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Follow the <a href={tutorialUrl}>tutorial</a> to configure a model and run your first task.</li>
      <li>Add your DeepSeek API key under <strong>Settings → Models</strong>.</li>
      <li>Build your own plugins with the <a href={pluginsUrl}>plugin guide</a>, or browse the full <a href="/plugins/directory/">tested plugin directory</a>.</li>
    </ol>
    <AdBanner />
  </section>
</Base>
